    "summary": "Out-of-bounds read in the HTTP stream wrapper when following a redirect with an empty Location header",
    "description": "### Summary\r\n\r\nWhen the HTTP stream wrapper follows a redirect and the response carries a `Location` header with an empty value, the redirect code reads one byte past the end of the heap buffer holding the location. The value of that out-of-bounds byte decides which redirect target is built, so a malicious server controls whether the client is sent to the host root or to the current directory.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\n\r\nSince the fix for GHSA-52jp-hrpf-2jff (CVE-2025-1861), `php_stream_http_response_headers_parse()` stores the `Location` value in a heap buffer of exactly `location_len + 1` bytes:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/php/php-src/blob/a66f30d78e10773048720b4b5f279136fdd0a433/ext/standard/http_fopen_w",
